{
    "background_story": "Babe was a majestic Tridacnidae, a giant clam that called the vibrant coral reef home. For decades, she filtered the crystal-clear waters, growing to an impressive size and becoming a beloved fixture in the reef community. Fish would dart in and out of her massive shell, and sea turtles would rest in the shade of her mantle. Babe's unique ability to photosynthesize through her symbiotic algae made her a vital part of the reef's ecosystem. As the reef faced threats from pollution and climate change, Babe remained a steadfast presence, her shell a symbol of resilience and adaptability. Her longevity and gentle nature earned her the respect and admiration of the entire reef, and she continued to thrive, a true giant of the ocean.",
